WEBVTT

1
00:00:01,401 --> 00:00:06,306
♪♪

2
00:00:11,411 --> 00:00:16,651
♪♪

3
00:00:18,118 --> 00:00:21,054
[Siren wailing in distance]

4
00:00:30,865 --> 00:00:33,400
[Phone buzzing]

5
00:00:43,878 --> 00:00:45,713
[Static]

6
00:00:48,282 --> 00:00:49,584
[Buzzing stops]

7
00:00:53,888 --> 00:00:55,422
[Static stops]

8
00:00:59,059 --> 00:01:01,428
[Phone buzzing]

9
00:01:06,768 --> 00:01:08,068
[Buzzing stops]

10
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:33,126
[Phone buzzing]

11
00:01:48,308 --> 00:01:50,845
-Dude, you have to
pick up your phone!

12
00:01:52,145 --> 00:01:54,414
Todd?

13
00:01:54,515 --> 00:01:55,917
Oh, my...

14
00:01:56,017 --> 00:01:58,318
Okay, Todd. Uh...

15
00:01:58,418 --> 00:02:02,023
Uh, hi. Um, I need help.
I need an ambulance.

16
00:02:02,122 --> 00:02:04,324
My brother isn't breathing.

17
00:02:04,826 --> 00:02:07,895
Uh, no, no, he's not --
he's not responding.

18
00:02:07,996 --> 00:02:09,964
He's unconscious. I...

19
00:02:10,064 --> 00:02:11,633
I don't know. I don't know.
I just --

20
00:02:11,733 --> 00:02:13,968
I just found him like this.
Something is really wrong.

21
00:02:14,068 --> 00:02:17,839
♪♪

22
00:02:17,939 --> 00:02:20,008
[Puppy squeaking]

23
00:02:20,108 --> 00:02:27,782
♪♪

24
00:02:27,882 --> 00:02:29,617
-Go get it. Go get it.

25
00:02:30,718 --> 00:02:32,386
Yeah. Fetch it up.

26
00:02:33,788 --> 00:02:36,124
What's up, man?
What are you looking at?

27
00:02:36,223 --> 00:02:39,393
[Laughing]

28
00:02:39,493 --> 00:02:44,398
Who's my bestest friend?
You? Is it you?

29
00:02:44,498 --> 00:02:46,968
You're so cute! I could die!

30
00:02:47,068 --> 00:02:52,740
♪♪

31
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:54,509
[Laughter]

32
00:02:54,609 --> 00:02:56,678
-Silly boy!

33
00:02:58,311 --> 00:03:01,115
-Aww! You're so cute!

34
00:03:01,214 --> 00:03:03,183
-What? Too scary for you?

35
00:03:03,283 --> 00:03:04,819
-[Indy barking]
-Indy! Come on!

36
00:03:04,919 --> 00:03:06,521
There's nothing there!

37
00:03:06,621 --> 00:03:08,923
[Coughing]

38
00:03:09,023 --> 00:03:10,525
-Look who's here!

39
00:03:10,625 --> 00:03:13,961
-Aww. There's my bestest friend.
Look at him. Look at him.

40
00:03:14,062 --> 00:03:15,830
Look at that big boy.

41
00:03:15,930 --> 00:03:17,832
[Chuckles]

42
00:03:17,932 --> 00:03:20,333
-Is that Papa? [Gasps]

43
00:03:20,434 --> 00:03:23,236
[Gasps] Who's that?

44
00:03:23,336 --> 00:03:25,372
He's free!

45
00:03:25,472 --> 00:03:29,911
Oh, the boys are back!

46
00:03:31,679 --> 00:03:33,748
[Todd barking]

47
00:03:36,084 --> 00:03:37,785
[Rain falling]

48
00:03:39,687 --> 00:03:41,321
[Phone buzzes]

49
00:03:53,901 --> 00:03:55,469
[Phone buzzing]

50
00:04:00,141 --> 00:04:02,242
-Okay.

51
00:04:02,342 --> 00:04:06,246
Nope. Stay here, boy.
Stay. Sit.

52
00:04:07,115 --> 00:04:09,316
Good boy. Stay.

53
00:04:11,119 --> 00:04:12,452
Hey, sis. Question for you.

54
00:04:12,553 --> 00:04:14,155
<i>-Todd, what the hell</i>
<i>is going on?</i>

55
00:04:14,254 --> 00:04:16,057
-Nothing.
<i>-I'm standing in your</i>

56
00:04:16,157 --> 00:04:17,357
<i>empty apartment right now.</i>

57
00:04:17,457 --> 00:04:19,127
-Oh, yeah.
That's why I called.

58
00:04:19,227 --> 00:04:20,528
Um, I decided to
get out of town for a bit.

59
00:04:20,628 --> 00:04:23,463
Do you know where
Grandpa hid the gate key?

60
00:04:23,564 --> 00:04:25,666
<i>-You're at Grandpa's?</i>

61
00:04:25,767 --> 00:04:27,101
-Do you know where
he hid the key or not?

62
00:04:27,201 --> 00:04:28,803
<i>-Are you out of your mind?!</i>

63
00:04:28,903 --> 00:04:31,072
<i>There is no way that</i>
<i>the doctor said this was okay!</i>

64
00:04:31,172 --> 00:04:32,774
-They discharged me,
didn't they?

65
00:04:32,874 --> 00:04:34,942
<i>-To go home, idiot!</i>

66
00:04:35,042 --> 00:04:37,111
<i>You can't just go wherever</i>
<i>the hell you want anymore!</i>

67
00:04:37,211 --> 00:04:39,080
-They keys, Vera.
Where are the keys?

68
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:41,082
<i>-Why Grandpa's?</i>
-Why not?

69
00:04:41,182 --> 00:04:43,951
[Indistinct conversation]

70
00:04:46,087 --> 00:04:49,289
-Exactly. It's available.
I'm not bothering anybody.

71
00:04:49,389 --> 00:04:52,459
I needed a break.
This could be good for me.

72
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:54,195
[Indistinct conversation]

73
00:04:54,294 --> 00:05:00,868
♪♪

74
00:05:00,968 --> 00:05:03,638
♪♪

75
00:05:03,738 --> 00:05:05,139
Found 'em!

76
00:05:05,239 --> 00:05:07,307
<i>-Okay, I need you close</i>
<i>in case something goes wrong.</i>

77
00:05:07,407 --> 00:05:08,976
-I gotta go.
Call me when you calm down.

78
00:05:09,076 --> 00:05:11,179
<i>-Wait! Wait, wait!</i>
<i>Just tell me that you're oka--</i>

79
00:05:11,279 --> 00:05:13,781
[Footsteps approach]

80
00:05:16,217 --> 00:05:18,351
-[Door closes]
-Enough of that.

81
00:05:18,451 --> 00:05:20,822
[Seat belt clicks]
Let's go.

82
00:05:33,234 --> 00:05:35,269
♪♪

83
00:05:35,368 --> 00:05:37,004
[Thunder rumbling]

84
00:05:37,104 --> 00:05:44,011
♪♪

85
00:05:45,246 --> 00:05:46,647
<i>[Man speaking on radio]</i>

86
00:05:46,747 --> 00:05:48,616
<i>-There'll be a lot</i>
<i>of cleaning up to do</i>

87
00:05:48,716 --> 00:05:50,618
<i>because of the weather</i>
<i>over the next couple of days.</i>

88
00:05:50,718 --> 00:05:52,520
<i>It should help out</i>
<i>that at least Thursday</i>

89
00:05:52,620 --> 00:05:54,354
<i>and Friday will be dryer.</i>

90
00:05:54,454 --> 00:05:57,525
<i>More rain comes in</i>
<i>on Friday night...</i>

91
00:05:57,625 --> 00:05:59,126
<i>[Speaking indistinctly]</i>

92
00:05:59,227 --> 00:06:00,695
[Phone buzzes]

93
00:06:03,831 --> 00:06:06,399
<i>[Man speaking indistinctly]</i>

94
00:06:13,808 --> 00:06:19,513
♪♪

95
00:06:21,381 --> 00:06:30,691
♪♪

96
00:06:30,791 --> 00:06:39,634
♪♪

97
00:06:39,734 --> 00:06:48,976
♪♪

98
00:06:51,411 --> 00:06:53,413
[Engine shuts off]

99
00:07:03,157 --> 00:07:05,192
-Come on, bud. Let's go.

100
00:07:06,661 --> 00:07:08,428
Come on, scaredy pants.

101
00:07:08,529 --> 00:07:10,197
[Indy grunts]

102
00:07:10,298 --> 00:07:11,933
It's not that bad.

103
00:07:13,167 --> 00:07:14,568
Come on, buddy.

104
00:07:15,603 --> 00:07:18,606
[Whistles]
You coming out or not?

105
00:07:22,176 --> 00:07:26,247
There we go! Okay.

106
00:07:26,347 --> 00:07:28,916
This way. Come on.

107
00:07:56,010 --> 00:07:58,045
[Dog whimpers]

108
00:07:59,947 --> 00:08:01,949
[Dog whimpers]

109
00:08:03,451 --> 00:08:05,553
[Lock clicks]

110
00:08:24,105 --> 00:08:25,973
Come on, bud. [Whistles]

111
00:08:29,210 --> 00:08:31,012
Okay.

112
00:08:31,112 --> 00:08:32,113
Welcome home.

113
00:08:32,213 --> 00:08:33,514
[Indy whimpers]

114
00:08:33,614 --> 00:08:34,949
I know!

115
00:08:35,049 --> 00:08:37,785
But it beats the hospital,
right?

116
00:08:39,020 --> 00:08:40,287
[Scoffs]

117
00:08:41,422 --> 00:08:42,923
[Sighs]

118
00:08:44,492 --> 00:08:46,227
Wait here.

119
00:09:03,010 --> 00:09:11,685
♪♪

120
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:28,135
♪♪

121
00:09:30,604 --> 00:09:32,973
[Thunder rumbles]

122
00:09:35,409 --> 00:09:44,852
♪♪

123
00:09:44,952 --> 00:09:53,094
♪♪

124
00:09:53,194 --> 00:09:54,962
Ohh! Man!

125
00:10:04,271 --> 00:10:05,739
[Clicking]

126
00:10:09,143 --> 00:10:10,911
[Sighs]

127
00:10:11,011 --> 00:10:12,446
Okay.

128
00:10:12,547 --> 00:10:14,516
Ohh! Yes.

129
00:10:14,615 --> 00:10:16,350
[Crackling]

130
00:10:18,553 --> 00:10:20,654
[Sighs]

131
00:10:21,822 --> 00:10:24,458
Something smells awful
down here.

132
00:10:24,559 --> 00:10:26,894
Glad I don't have <i>your</i> nose.

133
00:10:28,496 --> 00:10:30,297
Come on, bud.

134
00:10:36,237 --> 00:10:38,772
<i>-So, how long have you</i>
<i>been planning this?</i>

135
00:10:38,873 --> 00:10:42,810
-Planning? No planning.
It wasn't some big thing, Vera.

136
00:10:42,910 --> 00:10:44,579
<i>-The red light's on.</i>
-I just needed to go.

137
00:10:44,678 --> 00:10:46,780
<i>-Hm. No. Yeah.</i>
<i>That totally makes sense.</i>

138
00:10:46,881 --> 00:10:50,552
<i>The cursed family house</i>
<i>is a great place to relax.</i>

139
00:10:50,651 --> 00:10:53,187
-It's not really
how I remember it.

140
00:10:53,287 --> 00:10:54,889
<i>-Oh, yeah. Creepier?</i>

141
00:10:54,989 --> 00:10:56,690
-Not exactly. It's just...

142
00:10:56,790 --> 00:10:58,659
You think "house in the woods"
sounds so peaceful.

143
00:10:58,759 --> 00:11:00,794
<i>-[Dog barking]</i>
<i>-Wait. Is that Indy?</i>

144
00:11:00,895 --> 00:11:02,597
-No. Old home movie.

145
00:11:02,696 --> 00:11:04,298
Grandpa's playing fetch
with Bandit.

146
00:11:04,398 --> 00:11:05,432
You remember that dog?

147
00:11:05,534 --> 00:11:06,934
<i>-Uh, kinda.</i>

148
00:11:07,034 --> 00:11:09,003
<i>But didn't Grandpa</i>
<i>just have a ton of dogs?</i>

149
00:11:09,103 --> 00:11:11,640
-Yeah, but they all
just kept running away.

150
00:11:11,739 --> 00:11:13,608
Indy, on the other hand,
never leaves my side.

151
00:11:13,707 --> 00:11:15,342
I can't poop without a witness.

152
00:11:15,442 --> 00:11:18,012
<i>-Eww! Don't tell me that.</i>
<i>I don't need to know that.</i>

153
00:11:18,112 --> 00:11:19,680
<i>-[Dog barking]</i>
<i>-[Shouting]</i>

154
00:11:19,780 --> 00:11:21,982
-Grandpa had a ton
of these VHS tapes.

155
00:11:22,082 --> 00:11:25,819
Mostly this
and shitty horror films.

156
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:28,189
I think he was taping over them.

157
00:11:28,289 --> 00:11:30,659
<i>-What's the point</i>
<i>of making a home</i>
<i>movie if you live alone?</i>

158
00:11:30,758 --> 00:11:32,860
-No idea.

159
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:34,695
<i>-Can you tell there's</i>
<i>something wrong with him?</i>

160
00:11:34,795 --> 00:11:36,665
-Wrong with who?

161
00:11:36,764 --> 00:11:38,966
<i>-With Grandpa. On the tape.</i>

162
00:11:39,066 --> 00:11:42,369
-Not at all. He seems happy.

163
00:11:43,070 --> 00:11:46,207
<i>-Well, that's how Grandpa's</i>
<i>generation did it, you know?</i>

164
00:11:46,307 --> 00:11:47,875
<i>Put on a happy face,</i>

165
00:11:47,975 --> 00:11:50,945
<i>even when you're rotting</i>
<i>from the inside out, right?</i>

166
00:11:52,547 --> 00:11:54,683
<i>I guess living in a haunted</i>
<i>house takes your mind off it.</i>

167
00:11:54,782 --> 00:11:56,750
-The house
isn't haunted, Vera.

168
00:11:56,850 --> 00:11:59,286
<i>-Oh, yeah? No one has</i>
<i>lived there for more</i>
<i>than a few weeks.</i>

169
00:11:59,386 --> 00:12:02,723
-Grandpa did.
<i>-Yeah, and it killed him.</i>

170
00:12:04,825 --> 00:12:07,562
<i>Look, uh...</i>
<i>you just have to promise me</i>

171
00:12:07,662 --> 00:12:09,430
<i>that at the first sign</i>
<i>of relapse,</i>

172
00:12:09,531 --> 00:12:12,733
<i>you're gonna get in that car</i>
<i>and you are coming back.</i>

173
00:12:12,833 --> 00:12:14,935
-Okay. Sure.
But the rehab promised me...

174
00:12:15,035 --> 00:12:17,071
[Speaking indistinctly]

175
00:12:18,472 --> 00:12:20,007
<i>-Okay.</i>

176
00:12:21,475 --> 00:12:23,110
[Creaking]

177
00:12:26,814 --> 00:12:28,516
[Thunder rumbles]

178
00:12:39,226 --> 00:12:41,262
[Creaking]

179
00:12:43,598 --> 00:12:45,499
[Creaking]

180
00:12:58,178 --> 00:13:06,387
♪♪

181
00:13:06,487 --> 00:13:11,392
♪♪

182
00:13:11,492 --> 00:13:12,793
[Indy sniffing]

183
00:13:12,893 --> 00:13:14,529
[Creaking]

184
00:13:14,629 --> 00:13:19,967
♪♪

185
00:13:26,340 --> 00:13:27,875
[Click]

186
00:13:29,744 --> 00:13:36,718
♪♪

187
00:13:36,817 --> 00:13:39,621
♪♪

188
00:13:39,721 --> 00:13:41,221
[Click]

189
00:13:43,625 --> 00:13:45,593
-God damn it!

190
00:13:45,694 --> 00:13:51,599
♪♪

191
00:13:58,773 --> 00:14:00,407
[Creaking]

192
00:14:06,013 --> 00:14:08,115
[Thunder rumbles]

193
00:14:27,267 --> 00:14:29,236
[Creaking]

194
00:14:30,237 --> 00:14:31,338
Hey, man.

195
00:14:31,438 --> 00:14:32,906
[Indy whimpers]

196
00:14:33,006 --> 00:14:35,376
What's going on?

197
00:14:43,984 --> 00:14:46,186
Alright. Let's go.

198
00:14:46,286 --> 00:14:47,888
Come on.

199
00:14:49,123 --> 00:14:51,526
Come on. Come on.

200
00:14:51,626 --> 00:14:58,767
♪♪

201
00:14:58,867 --> 00:15:00,668
[Thunder rumbles]

202
00:15:11,579 --> 00:15:20,655
♪♪

203
00:15:20,755 --> 00:15:29,831
♪♪

204
00:15:29,930 --> 00:15:39,173
♪♪

205
00:15:39,273 --> 00:15:47,615
♪♪

206
00:15:47,715 --> 00:15:56,758
♪♪

207
00:15:56,858 --> 00:16:03,665
♪♪

208
00:16:03,765 --> 00:16:05,567
♪♪

209
00:16:05,667 --> 00:16:07,769
[Indy whimpers]

210
00:16:07,869 --> 00:16:09,504
What?

211
00:16:12,239 --> 00:16:14,441
Yeah. I know. It's creepy.

212
00:16:14,542 --> 00:16:17,110
It's all my family
buried under here.

213
00:16:17,211 --> 00:16:18,847
Come on. [Whistles]

214
00:16:18,947 --> 00:16:23,150
♪♪

215
00:16:23,250 --> 00:16:25,720
They all died pretty young, too.

216
00:16:25,820 --> 00:16:33,160
♪♪

217
00:16:33,260 --> 00:16:36,430
Whoa. Stay here, boy.

218
00:16:36,531 --> 00:16:45,272
♪♪

219
00:16:45,372 --> 00:16:47,742
♪♪

220
00:16:47,842 --> 00:16:49,577
[Urinating]

221
00:16:49,677 --> 00:16:56,116
♪♪

222
00:16:56,216 --> 00:16:58,352
[Indy whimpers]

223
00:16:58,452 --> 00:17:06,661
♪♪

224
00:17:06,761 --> 00:17:15,670
♪♪

225
00:17:15,770 --> 00:17:17,539
[Indy whimpers]

226
00:17:17,639 --> 00:17:26,346
♪♪

227
00:17:26,446 --> 00:17:29,684
♪♪

228
00:17:29,784 --> 00:17:31,418
-[Whistling]

229
00:17:39,159 --> 00:17:40,728
Here, boy.

230
00:17:44,431 --> 00:17:46,901
What the hell
are you doing out here?

231
00:17:47,001 --> 00:17:48,770
-Uh, excuse me?

232
00:17:48,870 --> 00:17:51,238
-You should be more careful.

233
00:17:51,338 --> 00:17:53,240
It's fox huntin' season.

234
00:17:53,340 --> 00:17:56,443
I've got traps and snares
all over these woods.

235
00:17:56,544 --> 00:17:59,446
-Is that Mr. Downs?
[Chuckles]

236
00:17:59,547 --> 00:18:01,783
-Good to see you all grown up.

237
00:18:01,883 --> 00:18:06,020
How long will you be staying
with us out here in the boonies?

238
00:18:06,153 --> 00:18:08,288
-Well, indefinitely.
I gave up my old place.

239
00:18:08,388 --> 00:18:10,058
Taking over Grandpa's.

240
00:18:10,157 --> 00:18:11,358
-You staying in that place?

241
00:18:11,458 --> 00:18:13,327
-Yeah. What?
-Nothing.

242
00:18:13,427 --> 00:18:16,030
I just pray for you
after everything,

243
00:18:16,129 --> 00:18:18,032
the way your grandpa died.

244
00:18:18,131 --> 00:18:19,634
-Well, we're gonna
make it our own.

245
00:18:19,734 --> 00:18:22,503
Just gotta clear it out,
get the electric going.

246
00:18:22,604 --> 00:18:25,238
-I got an old generator
if you need it.

247
00:18:25,339 --> 00:18:28,776
I'm just down the hill.
Come by any time you need help.

248
00:18:30,110 --> 00:18:33,447
Your grandpa was out here
with his dog, too.

249
00:18:35,516 --> 00:18:39,621
After we found his body,
we never did find that dog.

250
00:18:39,721 --> 00:18:41,121
[Soft growling]

251
00:18:45,560 --> 00:18:47,327
-Am I crazy?

252
00:18:47,427 --> 00:18:49,564
It's nice here, right?

253
00:18:51,099 --> 00:18:53,500
Right?

254
00:18:53,601 --> 00:18:56,436
Indy? Right?

255
00:19:01,843 --> 00:19:03,678
Yeah. You get it.

256
00:19:05,813 --> 00:19:07,347
Alright.

257
00:19:09,449 --> 00:19:11,986
-You're sure you know
how to set this up?

258
00:19:12,086 --> 00:19:14,022
Electric for old houses
is pretty tough.

259
00:19:14,122 --> 00:19:16,591
-Yeah. I got it.
Thank you, though.

260
00:19:16,691 --> 00:19:17,959
-Okay.

261
00:19:18,059 --> 00:19:19,192
Just make sure
you get it running

262
